            <ArticleTitle>Prediction of asthma in children at 6 and 12 years of age: Perth infant asthma follow-up study.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>44-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Longitudinal studies, starting in infancy, provide an opportunity to assess risk factors prior to long-term exposure to environmental factors. The status of the infant soon after birth is determined by genetic background and factors related to in utero influences. As a result of recent advances in molecular biology, the genetic component can now be evaluated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
